    "q-133265": {
      "dom_id": "question-133265",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14157242/assets/5bbf82f97549272635ff1ea78d945691cf356dfbde2d0933788f734d6b7f9601.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Fred's neighbor to the south, Emma, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+3x-10$ square meters, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Emma's plot of land is $x+5$ meters, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Emma's plot width is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nmeters.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+3x-10.$\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-10).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-10) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 10 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-5) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-10) & =-9 & \\times  \\\\ -1+10 & =9 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-5) & =-3 & \\times  \\\\ -2+5 & =3 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $3x=5x-2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3x-10 & ={x}^{2}+5x-2x-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x-2x-10 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x)+(-2x-10) & = \\\\ x(x+5)-2(x+5) & = \\\\ (x-2)(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x-2$ meters. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14157242/assets/6bdc252e1952c6e56a971c7d88c126a75a68e3ae48783c7cb65495ed5b4b86b1.png)",
