    "q-133407": {
      "dom_id": "question-133407",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14157242/assets/327db918054ccc7ac5cb70315023f4714b374994bded724b7451342dfac2d7ee.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            When $x=20\\,\\text{m},$ the dimensions of Emma's plot of land are $25\\,\\text{m}$ and $18\\text{m}.$ A water pipe goes diagonally from one corner to the opposite, as shown above. Find the **exact** length of the pipe.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The length of the pipe is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nmeters.",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have a right triangle with legs $a=25\\,\\text{m}$ and $b=18\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14157242/assets/4ac2862067c8e6e868b634003643ef935dbe652e3b46647466dd6b1dc2cb5172.png)\n\nLet $c$ be the length of the hypotenuse. Then, according to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={a}^{2}+{b}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values for $a$ and $b$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\sqrt{{25}^{2}+{18}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{625+324} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{949}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
